/-!
# Dimension inequality for finite type inclusions of Noetherian domains

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 02IJ, `algebra-lemma-dimension-formula`, inequality
clause (blueprint: lem-trf-affine-dimension-inequality).

Mathlib's residue field at a prime is a fraction field of the quotient by that prime.
Its canonical residue-field map supplies the coefficient algebra structure. Heights
are in `ℕ∞`; `Cardinal.toENat` preserves the finite transcendence degrees here.
The inequality is written with the residue transcendence degree on the left, so that
subtraction cannot truncate a negative right-hand side to zero.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

namespace Ideal

/-- Dimension inequality for a finite type inclusion of Noetherian commutative domains.
Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 02IJ, `algebra-lemma-dimension-formula`, inequality
clause (blueprint: lem-trf-affine-dimension-inequality).

Proof (the four steps of the DAG, following Tag 02IJ):
1. Put P = R[T]. By lem-weil-pbc-polynomial-ring-domain it is a domain. It is free
   over R, hence flat by lem-weil-pbc-projective-module-flat; it is finite type by
   def-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra, hence Noetherian by
   lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra-noetherian. Apply lem-weil-pbc-flat-height-formula
   to a prime over p. The domain tower identity
   lem-exc-domain-transcendence-degree-tower, applied through the fraction fields,
   gives trdeg_R P = 1 (def-kun-transcendence-degree).
2. Set D = R/p and F = Frac(D). Localizing D[T] at the nonzero elements of D gives
   F[T]: bring polynomial coefficients to a common denominator. Every prime below
   the fibre prime avoids these denominators. The prime correspondence of
   lem-weil-pbc-localization-prime-residue-field-iso therefore preserves all chains
   below it, its height, and its residue field. In F[T] the zero prime has height
   zero and residue transcendence degree one. By lem-pur-polynomial-field-pid every
   nonzero prime is maximal of height one, and its residue field is algebraic by
   lem-weil-pbc-simple-algebraic-extension-power-basis, hence of transcendence degree
   zero (def-kun-transcendence-degree). The two terms sum to one in either case.
   Substitution in step 1 gives equality for P.
3. For a one-generator quotient S = P/n with nonzero prime kernel n, injectivity
   on R means n contracts to zero. A nonzero polynomial in n makes the generator
   algebraic over Frac(R). The simple algebraic extension power-basis statement
   makes Frac(S) finite over Frac(R). For any s in S, linear dependence of its powers
   gives an annihilating polynomial over Frac(R); multiply by the product of its
   nonzero coefficient denominators to obtain one over R. Thus trdeg_R S = 0 by
   def-kun-transcendence-degree. The inverse image q' of q has the same residue field.
   Quotient prime correspondence identifies chains below q with chains from n to q'.
   Prefixing with the strict inclusion 0 < n gives ht(q) + 1 <= ht(q'). Apply step 2
   to q' and cancel one, giving the desired additive inequality for S.
4. Induct on the number of generators from def-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra.
   With none S = R, the primes and residue fields agree and both degrees vanish.
   With one generator the kernel of P -> S is zero or nonzero, giving steps 1-3.
   Otherwise let A be generated by all but the last generator and let r be the
   contraction of q. As a subring of S it is a domain; finite-type Noetherianity
   makes it Noetherian. Add the induction bound for R -> A and the one-generator
   bound for A -> S. Cancel the finite height of r. The field tower identity
   lem-kun-transcendence-degree-tower adds the residue degrees; the domain tower
   identity lem-exc-domain-transcendence-degree-tower adds the algebra degrees.
   This gives the displayed bound. Both heights are finite by Noetherianity and
   both degrees are finite by finite generation, so the additive bound is exactly
   the source's ordinary, nontruncated subtraction inequality.
-/
theorem height_add_trdeg_residueField_le
    {R : Type u} {S : Type v} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [IsDomain R] [IsDomain S]
    [Algebra R S] [IsNoetherianRing R] [Algebra.FiniteType R S]
    (hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap R S))
    (p : Ideal R) (q : Ideal S) [p.IsPrime] [q.IsPrime]
    (hpq : p = q.comap (algebraMap R S)) :
    q.height + Cardinal.toENat
        (@Algebra.trdeg p.ResidueField q.ResidueField _ _
          (Ideal.ResidueField.map p q (algebraMap R S) hpq).toAlgebra) ≤
      p.height + Cardinal.toENat (Algebra.trdeg R S) := by
  sorry

end Ideal
